  "note": "The Frostbite four were transcribed by hand from the course sheet; the rest were extracted from the same PDF by scripts/extract_courses.py, which parses the Frostbite page as a control and refuses to write unless it reproduces the hand transcription leg for leg. Mark ids key into config/marks.json, line ids into config/lines.json. Every leg targets exactly one mark and carries \"mark\" plus \"rounding\", except the last, which carries \"finish\": true and \"line\". There are no gates and no leg has two marks: Bricklanding 33A+33B and Smith+Lucky Bay 35A+35B are consecutive legs, each mark rounded on its own, and crossing between either pair while racing is a rule breach (DESIGN 6). Rounding is per leg, never taken from the mark default, because course 2 rounds club-32a to starboard on one pass and to port on another. Legs are ordered and repeat freely: course position is a leg index, never a mark identity. Where a sheet prints a shortened distance, shortened_at is the leg it resolves to, which can only be a leg returning to the line; where it resolves to none, shortened_at is absent and shortened_note says why (DESIGN 11.6).",
